    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Gemma3 images become indexed language-space embeddings",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Gemma3Config now reads a separate vision namespace. Required fields include attention heads, hidden width, patch size and mm_tokens_per_image. KV heads default to query heads; head dimension defaults to hidden_size // num_q_heads. Other fallbacks include 24 layers, intermediate width equal to hidden width and image size 896. Three RGB channels and LayerNorm epsilon 1e-6 are fixed in code; multimodal_projector_bias is stored but not consumed by the new assembly.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_548584d10c9a4ef88e1549ac8513de44",
              "call_3e67c98524c14cd19b4e1cde65219fa2",
              "call_b505de01527c4ce09f7ae1eeddd93308",
              "call_3d855a8d6f51498183157c6b0edcb99b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Configuration also unconditionally opens directory/preprocessor_config.json, requires image_processor_type == \"Gemma3ImageProcessor\", and reads image_mean, image_std, resample, rescale_factor and size. These settings are not optional merely because only the text component will subsequently be constructed.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_548584d10c9a4ef88e1549ac8513de44",
              "call_e33d4e849d3d47cebe447df61f21d1ce",
              "call_10e645ef0d604682820fdc3a931f8b97",
              "call_1258ba2e0e9b4bdc86d64ac87fcff2ef",
              "call_70b1b269d2554500bff5b57e9d71f9ac"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "preprocess converts transparency to white-backed RGB, resizes to its configured tuple, converts pixels to float32, multiplies by rescale_factor, then applies (image - mean) / std while channels are last. It finally transposes to channel-first, converts to half precision and adds batch dimension one. This is a single resized image path; the function adds no crop or multi-resolution expansion.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_548584d10c9a4ef88e1549ac8513de44",
              "call_d022e0ea3ab14746a9933d106be796a8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Whole-parent-tree searches found no existing preprocess/get_image_embeddings methods, Conv or PosEmbedding construction sites, ordinary MLP construction sites, or callers of the two image utilities. The new vision implementation therefore integrates previously exposed primitives rather than copying an established image workflow with additional guards.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_70b1b269d2554500bff5b57e9d71f9ac",
              "call_14eec8167554444dbc569ff856aea5c7",
              "call_927fc3c39c50416f8a814efff77d0b58",
              "call_6ff01d5d65f344c28a5de0567156bb59",
              "call_be7d78a8faf14c65bf9680083e5afed9"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The tower starts with a stride-equals-patch-size Conv, which flattens its spatial output into [batch, patches, hidden], followed by learned consecutive position vectors. Each encoder layer uses LayerNorm before attention and before an ordinary two-projection MLP, with residual additions supplied by TransformerBlock. Attention has no RoPE, and get_image_embeddings explicitly supplies causal=False. The inherited attention dispatcher selects uncached FlashAttention by default; its SDPA alternative permits this tower's absent sliding window and zero softcap.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_548584d10c9a4ef88e1549ac8513de44",
              "call_581cf55ece66405694d6847c7490bcf5",
              "call_e33b45c7a4ef4940b090236fdfc6dfb6",
              "call_e7cb53b6ec604481ab9b13854deb1fda",
              "call_748c95e5c7e94af3a4f753ac54e87466"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The MLP selects tanh-approximate GELU and pad_to=1. These choices work together: the checkpoint intermediate width is 4304, whereas default 128-element alignment would round it to 4352 and the down projection rejects unapproved input padding. Keeping exact dimensions avoids that constructor precondition rather than merely reducing storage.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_548584d10c9a4ef88e1549ac8513de44",
              "call_ca5debbe4b7245189b7f0f0bd1647843",
              "call_af1131ba1626423c9a9f4564fb6bdb74",
              "call_c6c3581fc79b4140befb0a7663bc6f4d"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "After post-LayerNorm, Gemma3MMPool transposes [B,P\u00b2,D] to channel-first spatial form, averages nonoverlapping square regions, and returns contiguous [B,T\u00b2,D]. The constructor derives P from image_size // patch_size and T from the integer square root of mm_tokens_per_image. A Gemma-style RMSNorm uses weight + 1, then Linear maps vision width to text width with transposed_load=False.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_548584d10c9a4ef88e1549ac8513de44",
              "call_61014b3fa80e4c1ca5a34439407ed1c9",
              "call_af1131ba1626423c9a9f4564fb6bdb74"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A bounded scalar transcription calculated 896/14 = 64 patches per side, 4096 patch tokens, 1152/16 = 72 channels per head, a pooling kernel/stride of 4 and 256 pooled tokens. It checked raster-order averaging on two synthetic channels and obtained [1,256,2]. The resulting image token string has 258 positions including its two boundaries. This was not execution of PyTorch pooling or the model.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_2c2edfb56f2c49d49fae2c35f30119b4"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "google/gemma-3-4b-it, google/gemma-3-4b-pt, google/gemma-3-4b-it-qat-int4-unquantized and google/gemma-3-4b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized each explicitly provide the same tower: hidden/intermediate widths 1152/4304, 27 layers, 16 heads, image size 896, patch size 14 and 256 image tokens. Each therefore overrides the layer/intermediate defaults, derives 72-wide heads and equal query/KV head counts, and projects to text width 2560. The QAT files explicitly agree with the fixed three channels, epsilon 1e-6 and selected GELU variant.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_c6c3581fc79b4140befb0a7663bc6f4d",
              "call_43ff457cb2594365abc53e4ed74c1267",
              "call_77501d7c2e3f4aa58d691d2500dfa21a",
              "call_ac6eb37f134f41699bd399a8be9df506",
              "call_548584d10c9a4ef88e1549ac8513de44"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "google/gemma-3-12b-it, google/gemma-3-12b-pt, google/gemma-3-12b-it-qat-int4-unquantized and google/gemma-3-12b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized each provide that same vision geometry and defaults, but project to text width 3840. google/gemma-3-27b-it, google/gemma-3-27b-pt and google/gemma-3-27b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized likewise share the tower and project to width 5376. The three QAT files explicitly agree with the fixed channel count, epsilon and activation selection.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_dc649946f096464c973d5fcf59b07ef0",
              "call_8bd1f7bb7bc44eb29ca973161b452d32",
              "call_8e82afeb4b1c4cefa9f2cfb515dc12ea",
              "call_63333c70196d4494a78039f99977a001",
              "call_8897baa9fe5a4235a2d780c700ccd188",
              "call_378da604a809439b84e7e357fe1aa784",
              "call_3f03f7acae004373a96426bb198d7ed4"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The 4B reference header contains patch weights [1152,3,14,14], patch bias [1152], positions [4096,1152], and all 27 layers' requested norm, q/k/v/out and fc1/fc2 weights and biases. Attention weights are [1152,1152]; fc1/fc2 weights are [4304,1152] and [1152,4304]. Post-LayerNorm and projector RMSNorm have width 1152. These vision tensors are all consumed by the assembly; pooling requests no checkpoint tensors.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_c4bbbf9e97b44c4d85a129a150602f31",
              "call_50df7cb4f1314337a58236a4619e3cce",
              "call_548584d10c9a4ef88e1549ac8513de44",
              "call_5ac945500a954f189dc6216283e4694c"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The reference projector is stored as mm_input_projection_weight with shape [1152,2560], [1152,3840] or [1152,5376] for the inspected 4B, 12B and 27B checkpoints. The existing header normalization changes that spelling to mm_input_projection.weight; transposed_load=False then preserves its input-by-output orientation. The sampled headers contain no projector bias or FP8 scale alongside these weights, so those optional reads have no supplied tensor. No alternate projector key is configured.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_c4bbbf9e97b44c4d85a129a150602f31",
              "call_19b7b8119f5d4f0ab5b2dc79efa80005",
              "call_e77d0f1a5d1d4bce8cbf520609e266dc",
              "call_02d95f143dac476e9fa5a812f1b9eedd",
              "call_af1131ba1626423c9a9f4564fb6bdb74",
              "call_548584d10c9a4ef88e1549ac8513de44"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The header-normalization ancestor records a collision when both projector spellings occur. That normalization remains unchanged in the inspected parent and is not repaired by this task; the inspected reference projector entries instead use the legacy spelling alone.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_02d95f143dac476e9fa5a812f1b9eedd",
              "call_c4bbbf9e97b44c4d85a129a150602f31",
              "call_19b7b8119f5d4f0ab5b2dc79efa80005",
              "call_e77d0f1a5d1d4bce8cbf520609e266dc",
              "call_548584d10c9a4ef88e1549ac8513de44"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "get_image_embeddings runs the tower noncausally, moves the result to CPU and removes its batch dimension. It constructs <start_of_image>, one -1 placeholder per vector, and <end_of_image>. MMEmbedding replaces placeholders with allocated synthetic IDs. Existing tokenization expands aliases to that token list, and Embedding.forward can replace synthetic IDs with the supplied vectors without applying the text embedding's square-root-width normalization to them.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_548584d10c9a4ef88e1549ac8513de44",
              "call_40dca287017b4fcf979309ddf839766b",
              "call_02f657a704c844b2aa0344dcc315788f",
              "call_988bfe927e8643d293119b4c93f8f657"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The autosplit hook now returns a half-precision [1,3,height,width] image probe instead of token IDs. Model._load_autosplit uses that metadata before loading and forwarding each module. Its dummy forwards use empty parameters, unlike get_image_embeddings' explicit causal=False, so the hook establishes input shape compatibility but not equivalent attention semantics during probing.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_548584d10c9a4ef88e1549ac8513de44",
              "call_10e645ef0d604682820fdc3a931f8b97",
              "call_748c95e5c7e94af3a4f753ac54e87466"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
